    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20542" root="سلم" body-key="s">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَلْمَى</span></b>  <i>A certain plant</i> (K, TA) <i>which becomes
green in the</i> [<i>season called</i>] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَيْف</span> [app. here
meaning <i>spring</i>]. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَبُو سَلْمَى</span> <i>The</i> [<i>species
of lizard called</i>] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَزَغ</span>: (K:) or, some say, [as
is said in the M,] ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَبُو سَلْمَانَ</span></b> . (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  See
also the next paragraph. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  [In the CK, by a
mistranscription, a meaning belonging to <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سُلَامَى</span>
is assigned to <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَلْمَى</span>.]

